This directory contains the cards used by the MadGraph5_aMC@NLO
fNLO fixed-order calculation.

Processes with on-shell decay chains additionally contain decay_card.dat.
That card controls the physical widths, dummy-width ratio, decay
renormalization scales, the production renormalization-scale momentum choice,
and NLO_COMBINATION_MODE. Full NLO production-and-decay bundles require
separate LO and NLO total widths for each corrected species. ADDITIVE is the
default and keeps their strict fixed-order O(alpha_s) expansion: all
narrow-width denominators use the LO entries and NLO-minus-LO enters only
through the linear Born counterterm. MULTIPLICATIVE combines the complete NLO
distribution of every factorized block and uses NLO total widths for corrected
decays. Its block cross terms are beyond NLO but do not constitute a complete
NNLO calculation.

  NLO_COMBINATION_MODE ADDITIVE
  # or: NLO_COMBINATION_MODE MULTIPLICATIVE

MULTIPLICATIVE_VIRTUAL_FRACTION controls unbiased stochastic sampling of the
complete virtual residual. Its default is 1.0 (evaluate every virtual). A
value p in (0,1) uses one Bernoulli mask shared by every production/decay tuple
and every scale/PDF weight at an integration point, evaluating
W_no-virtual + I/p (W_full - W_no-virtual). This option is valid only in
MULTIPLICATIVE mode; all real and integrated subtraction pieces remain
deterministic.

For loop_sm and loop_sm-no_b_mass, virtual corrections to an on-shell
t -> b W+ or t~ -> b~ W- block use the bundled analytic CDR spin-density
matrix. This applies both when the W is external to the block and when its
decay leaves its spin index open. Each generated provider first compares all
complex finite, single-pole, and double-pole density entries against MadLoop
at two distinct boosted block-local phase-space points and stops on a
discrepancy. It then uses the analytic result at every subsequent point.
These fast decay virtuals are never sampled or replaced by an approximation;
production virtuals retain the configured virtual treatment. Unsupported
models and decay topologies continue to use MadLoop normally.

FORMAT 5 adds explicit decay-scale variations:

  DECAY_SCALE_VARIATION_MODE CORRELATED
  DECAY_SCALE_FACTORS 3 1.0 2.0 0.5
  LO_DECAY_WIDTH_VARIATION 6 2.0 <LO width at 2 mu_decay>
  NLO_DECAY_WIDTH_VARIATION 6 2.0 <NLO width at 2 mu_decay>
  LO_DECAY_WIDTH_VARIATION 6 0.5 <LO width at mu_decay/2>
  NLO_DECAY_WIDTH_VARIATION 6 0.5 <NLO width at mu_decay/2>

Use CORRELATED to identify the decay factors with rw_rscale; the factor lists
must then match exactly and in the same order. Use INDEPENDENT for the full
Cartesian product of production muR, production muF, and one factor per
distinct scale-dependent decay species. The first factor must be 1. Every
non-central point needs an explicit LO total width for each varied species
and an explicit NLO total width for each NLO-corrected species. Missing widths
are a fatal input error; they are never inferred by running or rescaling a
central width.

The run-card switch cut_decays controls whether built-in and user-defined
generation cuts see forced-decay products. It defaults to false; fixed-order
analyses always see the complete decayed event.
